id: pm-gh1614
title: "GH-1614: keep typed SDK data literal across CLI sentinel inputs"
description: "GitHub https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1614 reports typed PmClient fields consuming CLI sentinels. A sandboxed current-source Node24 probe with closed stdin reproduces description '-' becoming empty and assignee 'none' being removed. Typed integrations can silently rewrite provider payloads. Audit create/update/append and separate literal typed input from explicit CLI stdin, file and clear transport syntax, retaining documented unset APIs and CLI compatibility."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T17:43:51.501Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T18:12:31.905Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Literal SDK text fields preserve sentinel spellings through create/update/append; SDK data calls do not implicitly consume stdin or read files; Explicit typed clear/unset and existing CLI transport semantics retain focused conformance tests
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: high
confidence: high
expected_result: Typed SDK string data round-trips sentinel spellings without implicit stdin/file reads; explicit unset remains typed and CLI sentinel behavior retains focused conformance evidence.
